<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προαφ-ίσταμαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		, with pf. and aor. 2
		
			Act.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>secede, revolt
				before,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.12
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>leave off</i> or <i>desist before,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				175d
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ π., πρὶν ἂν . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					85c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπαντα . . ἐξευρίσκεται, ἂν μὴ
					προαποστῇς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					30.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>depart from before,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ὅπλων -αποστῆναι,</span> of
			soldiers laying down arms, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				49.41
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
